A dark cloud of Strix envolop the company
A cacophony of flapping, and whistling as they plummit in angled dives
Some Men are struck, as if stuck by lightning. 
There is raking of talons within the a singular flickering shadow blotting out the summer noon
Alik strides into the fray, mud flecking onto his gleaming plate armor.
Held firmly in one hand, tucked against his shoulder, his war hammer. The head gliding just an inch above the mud
Gripped in the other, a chain leash, held short to restrain the eager man at its end
Alik looks up at the vicious creature now whistling towards him
He releases the chain, and it unfurls from where it was looped at his side
Exploding from the earth, the Hound hurtles into the air and latches onto the beast, still 30 feet from its' armored target
With a shriek, one of the Strix' wings is ripped from its body, and it now tumbles wildly through the sky
The hound leaps clear of his victim, and Alik hefts his hammer
A mighty swing intercepts the one-winged strix, and it explodes in a cloud of feathers and gore
The now stringy corpse sails away, while that wing, spasming, kicks up mud in front of Alik
Under blood misted visor, he half-smiles, testing the weight of his hammer in his hands
The chain whips taught, and he pulled forward by one arm, iron boots sliding through the mud
In the sky, like a human kite, the hound has reached end of his leash
With a curse, Alik pulls the hound, clawing and scrabbling as he falls through a cloud of bloody feathers
A forcefully-driven spear glances off Aliks shoulder
His hammer splashes to the ground as he catches the assailants' foot and rips it from the sky
Alik backhands the creature with his gauntlet, then stomps it into the ground